## Data Structure and Identifiers

MoBa data are distributed across multiple datasets and must be linked prior to analysis.

### Core identifiers

- `PREG_ID` – Pregnancy ID  
- `BARN_NR` – Child number within pregnancy  
- `M_ID` – Mother ID  
- `F_ID` – Father ID  

> **Important:**  
> Identifiers are project-specific. The same individual will have different IDs across projects.

---

## Merging Files

Each questionnaire is delivered as separate data files.

### Before birth (pregnancy data)
- Use: `PREG_ID`
- Applies to:
  - Q1, QF (week 15–17)
  - Q2 (week 22)
  - Q3 (week 30)

### After birth (child data)
- Use: `PREG_ID` + `BARN_NR`
- Required for correct linkage (especially twins/triplets)
- Applies to:
  - Q4, Q5, Q6, Q5Y, Q7Y, etc.

### Special case: Father questionnaire (QF2)
- Part 1 (father): use `F_ID`
- Part 2 (child): use `PREG_ID` + `BARN_NR`

🔗 See syntax examples: [Merge files](Merge%20files.md#merge-files)

### Important considerations

- Not all participants completed all questionnaires  
- Missing values may reflect non-participation (not just missing responses)

`SV_INFO`:
- Contains `M_ID`
- Can be used to identify mothers with multiple pregnancies (siblings)

